When is $n+1$ divisible by 3? When $n \equiv 2 \pmod 3$.
When is $n-1$ divisible by 3? When $n \equiv 1 \pmod 3$.
If $n \equiv 0 \pmod 3$, neither $n+1$ nor $n-1$ is divisible by 3.

